{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeRB4e5Riie8c3uY2Kq5W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Root cause:** It's a source-code bug, not a routing-table issue.\n\n`routes/public.map` is correct — it lists `/health` before the `/*` wildcard, so the mapping intends `/health` to resolve to the `health` handler.\n\nThe bug is in `router/routes.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc HealthHandler() string { return \"wildcard\" }\n```\n\n`HealthHandler` is hard-coded to return `\"wildcard\"` instead of `\"health\"`. So regardless of how `public.map` routes requests, the handler function itself returns the wrong value — effectively behaving as if `/health` were shadowed by the wildcard route, even though the map file correctly orders `/health` before `/*`.\n\n**Fix** (in `router/routes.go`, not `routes/public.map`): change the return value to `\"health\"`:\n\n```go\nfunc HealthHandler() string { return \"health\" }\n```\n\nThis will make `TestHealthRoute` pass without touching `routes/public.map`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":3348,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28280ed4-3ab2-4e83-9278-5bf55f5447af","uuid":"5b24ad05-556b-443e-a9cb-2a515c431e04","timestamp":"2026-08-26T10:07:13.801Z","request_id":"req_011CeRB4d6thi1hftyvHwLB9"}
